A||||8||wkayl||What NOT to see in the headlights...||||6||
Z||000000||wkayl||04-11-2000||09:55 PM||||I took a 600 mile round-trip from Loveland CO Sunday evening to Spearfish SD and back.  Here is what I saw in Spearfish Canyon at about 1:00 in the morning.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deerthree.jpg"> <P>More pictures of the trip:  <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/headlights.html</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||sdm1964||04-11-2000||10:19 PM||||no kidding, or the way i see it, we are so low to the ground we would take the legs right out and the body would go over the top and not touch the roof.||||reg||11
Z||000002||TheFiero64||04-12-2000||05:02 PM||||That really scares me. This is what happened to me last year: <BR>My girlfriend and I were driving to a friends house in my 88 coupe(now v6). The roads were really icy, so I was driving slow.  A good song came on the radio, and we were singing along with it. All of a sudden we saw a flash of white on the right side of the car and felt the car hit something   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">.  It took us a few seconds to realize that a deer had run out of<BR>someone's driveway right into the front side of my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. I pulled over and realized that I only had one headlight sticking out of my hood. I thought my poor fiero was badly damaged in the front. I got out to assess the damage. My passenger side headlight is completely gone, The part that pivots up had ripped right off. the door to the light was also gone. There was some paint missing on the passenger side front bumper, the right fender had football size crack in it with fur sticking out. My antenna was bent over.<BR>When the antenna bent over,it hit the windshield and cracked it. My sidemarker light was gone. We were OK, just shaken up.  My girlfriend was practically hyperventilating, though.  I turned the car around(it was still drivable)and went back to check out the deer.  She was still alive and trying to get up, but she couldn't. I had to pick up peace's of my car everywhere. You could tell she was hurt. I told a neighbor to call the police. After the cop came, he told us he would have to put her down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  It was a very unfortunate thing to have happened, but we were very lucky.  If the deer hadn't hit where it did, we could've been badly hurt.  There also could've been a lot more damage to the car.  If you think about it, any other car would likely have been totaled, or at least badly damaged.  It's a strong car, the damage is<BR>definitely fixable. I got 650 dollars after my 500 dollar deductible and fixed it up better than before   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 04-12-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||batboy||04-12-2000||07:57 PM||||I have nightmares of hitting a deer, taking out the legs, having it slide up the hood, through the windshield, and land in my lap with it struggling, kicking, and biting because it's scared and injuried as we go careening off into a deep ditch or smacking a tree...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||04-12-2000||09:33 PM||||Those deer sirens are supposed to work||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||04-12-2000||11:18 PM||||I have close calls nearly everyday.  As I see it, my car has saved me from taking out a few deer because of its braking a handling characteristics.  Not to mention the dozens of other furry creatures I've managed to avoid.  I guess I've kind of developed a sixth sense for potential roadkill or maybe it's just the hours I've spent looking for deer and learning what areas they frequent during certain times and seasons.  That being said I nearly hit a doe today as I was going up through the gears.  She jumped out of the woods just as I got to about 45.  She was right beside me along the side of the road when she decided to turn around and go back into the woods.  You have to appreciate the speed of these animals.  Even though the one I saw today was right beside me when I saw her, I have no doubt that if she kept on going in that direction, my car would have a pretty good deer sized hole in it.  I am always on the lookout for deer, I've just gotta be.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiasco||04-13-2000||01:20 AM||||I live in the woods of Wisconsin and have hit my share of deer.(also muskrats, skunks, rabbits, you name it) Just when you think you know what they'll do, you get a nice little surprise and ALL FOUR deer that had just safely crossed the road ahead decide that no, "we liked the other side better" and run in front of you a second time. <BR>-Well two of them made it across in front of me this time. The fourth reversed directions AGAIN and ran back into the ditch. The third, however, ran directly into the right front fender of my sweet ride. ($150 Chevette with 230,000 miles) It kinda did a floppy Dukes O' Hazzard across the hood, cracked the windshield with a hoof, and landed on the road sorta on its side and legs. By this time I believe I had soiled myself. My new friend then got up and bounded off into a swamp.<BR>I know deer aren't all that bright, especially in rut, but why would you run straight AT the big, black, noisy thing barrelling down the road?  Stupid critters.<P>Haven't hit any in the Fiero yet but I'm sure it will happen. So save those parts-car body panels for me!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||04-13-2000||02:21 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> DAMN DEER!!!! I was driving in the forest preserve at 3:30am with a buddy in my 86 Mustang doing about 95mph  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> , when all I saw was a white flash go by and felt a minor thud   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> . I locked up the brakes and jumped out of the car to see a White deer standing on the side of the road. There was white fur stuck in my drivers mirror but no damage. So I guess I hit his tail??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> By the way I NEVER speed in the forest preserves (at night <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) anymore!! DAMN DEER!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <BR>  ||||reg||8
Z||000008||DJRice||04-13-2000||09:24 AM||||About a week before Christmas '98 I was headed home from work (in my Buick, thankfully) about 9:30pm.  The four lane road I was on was about to shrink to two lanes.  I saw a deer up ahead in the road and slowed down for it.  The next thing I know, BAM.  I took a hit to the drivers side rear door.  So I pull over to check it out.<P>The back door was smashed in real good.  As was the rear quarter panel.  And I had a bit of fur in on my bumper.  Had that been my Fiero, Id probably still be crying...||||reg||1
